{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477034-demonic-investment-flaws-for-op-nephilim","id":1477034,"title":"Demonic Investment Flaws for OP Nephilim","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-22T16:41:13-07:00","id":1477034,"title":"Demonic Investment Flaws for OP Nephilim","content":"I got a IMO thematically appropriate idea to boost the power of a demonic Nephilim/Laham character in an OP chronicle. Allow them to get several Demonic Investment Flaws with no limit (besides the usual 13-pts threshold for other Flaws) and full point benefits. They would be the ones that are listed in Book of the Fallen plus others that are required for Nephilim or seem thematically appropriate. They are side effects of the character's supernatural heritage, rather than coming from a soul-pact.<br /> <br /> Addiction (Fighting) (0/-3) (appropriate to the concept and set to 0-pts. as required for a Nephilim).<br /> Beast Within (-5) (appropriate to the concept).<br /> Bizarre Hunger (Rotten Food) (-3) (the universe has a sense of irony).<br /> Cast No Shadow or Reflection (-2) (very appropriate to the character).<br /> Cursed (Tech Malfunctions) (-5) (very appropriate to the technophobe aspect of the concept).<br /> Dark Secret (-1) (character has skeletons in the closet, beginning with their origin).<br /> Deranged (Sociopathy) (0/-5) (appropriate to the concept and set to 0-pts. as required for a Nephilim).<br /> Devil\u2019s Mark (-1) (appropriate to the concept).<br /> Diabolical Mentor (-2) (character was created and mentored by an Infernalist).<br /> Echoes (-5) (appropriate to the concept).<br /> Haunted (-3) (character tends to attract the wrong kind of attention from the Umbra).<br /> Icy (-2) (fits with Deranged: Sociopathy).<br /> Nightmares (-1) (character has an... interesting background).<br /> Primal Marks: (-3) (appropriate to the concept).<br /> Spirit Magnet (-7) (character tends to attract the wrong kind of attention from the Umbra).<br /> Strangeness (-1) (appropriate to the concept).<br /> Taint of Corruption (-7) (appropriate to the concept and very useful).<br /> Vulnerability (Weakness; Holy Objects) (-3) (nobody is perfect).<br /> <br /> Possible other Flaws that are not used:<br /> Aging (character is supposed to be Immortal and Unaging).<br /> Bedeviled (probably too risky given the high-stakes nature of the story).<br /> Bound (character made no soul pact, this stuff is innate).<br /> Catspaw (the character swore no soul pact and severed ties with their Infernalist creator/mentor).<br /> Dark Fate (for the same reasons as Bound).<br /> Degeneration (character is supposed to be Immortal and have Spark of Life).<br /> Horrific (character is supposed to be attractive and have Enchanting Features).<br /> Mayfly Curse (for the same reasons as other Flaws that compromise health or lifespan).<br /> Monstrous (for the same reasons as Horrific).<br /> Obsession (the character is not beholden to a soul pact).<br /> Paranormal Prohibition or Imperative (probably appropriate but character already has lots of Supernatural Flaws).<br /> Permanent Paradox Flaw (probably appropriate but character already has Echoes).<br /> Permanent Wound (for the same reasons as other Flaws that compromise health or lifespan).<br /> Psychic Vampire (character is supposed to have Spark of Life).<br /> Repulsive Feature (character is supposed to be attractive and have Enchanting Features).<br /> Uncanny (character is supposed to have Arcane, although the Flaw likely comes close to mandatory due to abundance of Supernatural Flaws).<br /> <br /> To provide context, these are the other tentative features of the character:<br /> <br /> Paradigm: Everything is Chaos and Might Makes Right, so Transcend Your Limits.<br /> <br /> Practices: Animalism, Bardism, Crazy Wisdom, Elementalism, Invigoration, Martial Arts, Medicine Work, Psionics, Witchcraft, and Yoga.<br /> <br /> Instruments: Bodywork; dance, gestures, and movement; energy; eye contact; language, music, and voice; math and numerology; meditation; ordeals and exertions; sex and sensuality; social domination.<br /> <br /> Affiliation: Sahajiva and Verbena.<br /> <br /> Preferred Spheres: Entropy, Forces, Life, Mind, Prime.<br /> <br /> Preferred Abilities: Alertness, Art, Athletics, Awareness, Empathy, Expression, Intimidation, Martial Arts, Meditation, Stealth, Survival, Academics (math), Cosmology, Enigmas, Esoterica, Medicine.<br /> <br /> Preferred Backgrounds: Arcane, Avatar, Dream.<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Artistically Gifted (1) (good for instruments).<br /> Cast-Iron Stomach (1) (necessary to deal with Bizarre Hunger).<br /> Dual Affiliation (7) (not sure if worth the cost, but paradigm kinda bridges two Traditions and the extra Affinity Sphere is nice to have).<br /> Enchanting Feature (x3) (Enchanting Gaze; Angelic Voice; Strong and Graceful Body) (6) (good for instruments and balancing the uncanny and awkward nature of the character).<br /> Hypersensitivity (3) (good for instruments).<br /> Immortal (7) (integral to the concept and fits the background).<br /> Lightning Calculator (1) (good for instruments).<br /> Natural Channel (3) (character has lots of affinity for the Umbra).<br /> Natural Shapeshifter (3) (it fits with Spark of Life and proficiency in the Life Sphere).<br /> Nephilim/Laham (7) (central to the concept and very useful).<br /> Self-Confident (5) (appropriate to paradigm and personality).<br /> Spark of Life (5) (appropriate to the concept and very useful).<br /> Unaging (2) (integral to the concept and fits the background).<br /> <br /> Equivalents of Stormwarden, Too Tough to Die, and Umbral Affinity at no cost due to optional/house rules.<br /> <br /> Special Advantages:<br /> Rapid Healing (x2) (0/4) (free for Nephilim and fits other Merits).<br /> Regrowth (1/4) (almost free for Nephilim and fits other Merits).<br /> <br /> Other Flaws (very tentative):<br /> Construct (-2) (character was created by an Infernalist).<br /> Curiosity (-2).<br /> Impatient (-1).<br /> Intemperate (-2).<br /> Offline (-3) (character has major trouble with technology).<br /> Phobia (Closed Spaces) (-3) (bad memories from early life with creator/mentor).<br /> <br /> A few of the above might possibly get replaced with Anachronism (alienation from society), Bigot (intolerance of Sleepers), Enemy, Gremlin, Hit List, Immortal Enemy, Inappropriate (alienation from society), Prone to Quiet, and/or Witch-Hunted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-29-2022, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}